coturn on FenrirOS
==================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and there is no configuration,
no realm, no user and no shared secret. Upstream's sample configuration is in
/usr/share/doc/coturn (turnserver.conf.default).

    cp /usr/share/doc/coturn/turnserver.conf.default /etc/coturn/turnserver.conf
    chgrp coturn /etc/coturn/turnserver.conf; chmod 640 /etc/coturn/turnserver.conf
    $EDITOR /etc/coturn/turnserver.conf   # realm, static-auth-secret (use-auth-secret), cert/pkey, listening ports
    dinitctl enable turnserver

For Matrix (Synapse turn_shared_secret), Jitsi and Nextcloud Talk use
use-auth-secret with a secret you generate (`openssl rand -hex 32`) and share
it with the application. Open 3478 (UDP/TCP), 5349 (TLS) and the relay port
range (min-port/max-port) in the firewall. The service runs as the coturn
user in the foreground. Data: /var/lib/coturn; logs: /var/log/turnserver.log.
